00:33:43.850 --> 00:33:45.930
All you got to do is talk, son, and you'll be out of here.

00:33:46.910 --> 00:33:49.130
Just tell us where we can collar them desperadoes.

00:33:50.260 --> 00:33:50.900
Try and remember.

00:33:51.190 --> 00:33:52.050
I tell you, I don't know.

00:33:53.680 --> 00:33:55.500
I'll be outside if you want to talk to me.

00:33:56.870 --> 00:33:57.410
Think it over.

00:34:06.520 --> 00:34:09.260
It wasn't worth ten years of your life, was it?

00:34:12.400 --> 00:34:14.060
Pop, where have you been? I've been looking all over for you.

00:34:14.180 --> 00:34:16.020
Oh, just around, my boy.

00:34:16.240 --> 00:34:18.120
Did I meet you last night, or did I dream it?

00:34:18.290 --> 00:34:19.470
Tell me, did you give me a newspaper?

00:34:19.710 --> 00:34:22.010
It didn't do you any good, did it, Larry?

00:34:22.370 --> 00:34:25.270
Oh, Pop, I'm in a jam. Nobody believes me. I can't get out of here.

00:34:26.120 --> 00:34:28.400
Why don't you say something? What are you looking at me like that for?

00:34:28.970 --> 00:34:29.870
I'm kind of surprised.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.440
Nice to see you here, that's all.

00:34:31.860 --> 00:34:34.360
I figured you'd be on your way to the river by this time.

00:34:34.680 --> 00:34:36.680
He ought to be there a little after midnight.

00:34:37.100 --> 00:34:37.920
You gotta be.

00:34:38.040 --> 00:34:38.640
Who says so?

00:34:39.310 --> 00:34:40.690
Why, I just read it.

00:34:40.870 --> 00:34:42.330
Don't tell me that's the next tomorrow's paper.

00:34:42.730 --> 00:34:44.070
Isn't that what you want?

00:34:44.250 --> 00:34:44.510
No!

00:34:44.930 --> 00:34:49.390
You want to tell me something?

00:34:49.470 --> 00:34:49.730
No.

00:34:50.810 --> 00:34:51.110
Yes.

00:34:52.080 --> 00:34:52.420
Maybe.

00:34:52.950 --> 00:34:59.620
Wait, does it say anything in the paper about those bandits?

00:35:02.490 --> 00:35:04.940
Well, here it is. They've been arrested.

00:35:05.260 --> 00:35:05.920
When were they? Where?

00:35:06.200 --> 00:35:08.440
Tomorrow morning, in the Union Bank.

00:35:08.980 --> 00:35:10.480
The police were waiting for them.

00:35:11.150 --> 00:35:11.930
You wrote that.

00:35:17.860 --> 00:35:18.460
What about me?

00:35:18.640 --> 00:35:19.820
Oh, you'll be a hero.

00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:21.060
For telling the police?

00:35:21.440 --> 00:35:24.740
Oh, no. I'd better read it to you.

00:35:25.900 --> 00:35:28.220
Unknown woman makes suicide leap.

00:35:28.920 --> 00:35:29.980
Jumps to death from...

00:35:30.030 --> 00:35:37.540
Street Bridge. Larry Stevens, evening news reporter, makes heroic attempt at

00:35:37.540 --> 00:35:43.390
rescue in river. Body not yet recovered. Shortly after midnight last night...

00:35:43.390 --> 00:35:48.030
Now I don't believe a word of it. Why, it says so here. But I'm being held here.

00:35:48.150 --> 00:35:52.580
I can't get away. Even if I could, I wouldn't go to the river. Even if I did, I wouldn't jump in.

00:35:52.970 --> 00:35:57.590
What kind of a monkey do you think I am to risk my life for a woman I don't know when I do know she can't be saved?

00:35:58.460 --> 00:35:59.780
Don't ask me, my boy.

00:36:00.440 --> 00:36:03.000
I'm no prophet. I'm just reading this.

00:36:03.080 --> 00:36:05.540
Enough! Enough! I never might have heard of that paper again!

00:36:06.640 --> 00:36:07.660
You're hollering for me.

00:36:07.900 --> 00:36:09.180
No, get out of here and leave me alone.

00:36:10.420 --> 00:36:13.800
Look, if you let me out, I'll tell you where you can get those bandits.

00:36:14.320 --> 00:36:15.320
Now we're getting somewhere.

00:36:15.460 --> 00:36:17.500
Tomorrow morning at the Union Bank. All you have to do is wait for them.

00:36:18.800 --> 00:36:19.620
Come along, mister.

00:36:29.100 --> 00:36:29.780
Right, Stevens.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.060
It's all right. We'll be waiting at the bank.

00:36:32.760 --> 00:36:35.880
But if you're fooling us, remember we know where to pick you up.

00:36:37.010 --> 00:36:37.730
You can go now.

00:36:37.890 --> 00:36:38.490
Thanks, Inspector.

00:36:39.210 --> 00:36:42.240
Oh, uh, where's Miss Smith? I order an apology.

00:36:43.580 --> 00:36:46.220
Miss Smith disappeared after the show, Mr. Stephen.

00:36:47.780 --> 00:36:49.700
Her uncle says he don't know where she's gone.

00:36:49.860 --> 00:36:51.620
That's right, I don't know, but he knows.

00:36:52.030 --> 00:36:53.890
Listen, this guy's trying to steal my niece.

00:36:54.010 --> 00:36:55.030
She's in fact a way to wit him.

00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:55.980
Say that again, please.

00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:57.140
Oh, listen, you young whippers.

00:36:57.280 --> 00:36:58.080
Step around, hit you over the head.

00:36:58.160 --> 00:36:59.920
All right, shut up, shut up the both of you.

00:37:01.760 --> 00:37:04.590
Before you go, Stevens, I'd like to get to the bottom of this.

00:37:05.110 --> 00:37:07.670
At what time did the girl tell you about the holdup?

00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:08.900
She didn't tell me at all.

00:37:09.020 --> 00:37:09.860
Of course she didn't.

00:37:09.860 --> 00:37:10.540
Now you're lying.

00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:11.540
Listen, I ain't lying.

00:37:11.760 --> 00:37:13.580
A couple of hours ago, you admitted it.

00:37:13.680 --> 00:37:15.160
I didn't know you was a police inspector.

00:37:15.380 --> 00:37:16.040
Oh, I see.

00:37:16.290 --> 00:37:17.110
Oh, you don't understand.

00:37:17.110 --> 00:37:18.790
I was just putting on an act for Blacksteen.

00:37:18.890 --> 00:37:20.130
That's Barnum and Bailey's big man.

00:37:20.250 --> 00:37:20.790
Don't you understand?

00:37:21.280 --> 00:37:22.100
Listen, how could you?

00:37:22.140 --> 00:37:23.100
You're an intelligent man.

00:37:23.180 --> 00:37:25.600
How could you believe that we could predict anything we don't know nothing about?

00:37:25.960 --> 00:37:27.400
And by the way, who heard the prediction?

00:37:27.580 --> 00:37:28.200
Did you hear it?

00:37:28.300 --> 00:37:28.940
I didn't.

00:37:29.690 --> 00:37:29.930
No.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.020
But I did hear the prediction tonight.

00:37:32.260 --> 00:37:34.120
Ah, that's bunk, Inspector, bunk.

00:37:34.540 --> 00:37:36.500
How could she know anything about a bridge and a river

00:37:36.500 --> 00:37:37.600
and a woman committing suicide?

00:37:37.860 --> 00:37:38.620
Now, how could she?

00:37:39.870 --> 00:37:41.700
Did Sylvia say that?

00:37:43.360 --> 00:37:43.860
Shut up.

00:37:43.960 --> 00:37:45.520
She was just trying to get us all out of a tight hole.

00:37:45.640 --> 00:37:46.060
You, too.

00:37:46.500 --> 00:37:47.840
Bridge? The river?

00:37:49.880 --> 00:37:52.260
Did she say the body would never be found?

00:37:52.640 --> 00:37:53.540
She didn't say that.

00:37:53.760 --> 00:37:54.020
No.

00:37:54.280 --> 00:37:54.880
She didn't know!

00:37:55.220 --> 00:37:58.620
What is this nonsense?

00:37:58.780 --> 00:37:59.660
Don't let that guy get away!

00:38:00.030 --> 00:38:01.310
You keep him in here if you know your business.

00:38:01.870 --> 00:38:04.420
If I know my business, you're coming with me.

00:38:04.600 --> 00:38:04.780
Wait!

00:38:32.880 --> 00:38:34.080
Somebody better dive in.

00:38:34.080 --> 00:38:34.700
That's the idea.

00:38:37.090 --> 00:38:38.030
Go ahead, jump.

00:38:38.210 --> 00:38:39.110
Oh, I can't swim.

00:38:39.490 --> 00:38:40.210
I can either.

00:38:40.330 --> 00:38:40.970
Neither can I.

00:38:41.350 --> 00:38:42.310
Oh, officer, officer.

00:38:44.320 --> 00:38:44.760
Can you see her?

00:38:44.880 --> 00:38:46.540
No, no, we can't see anything.

00:38:47.720 --> 00:38:49.200
Then there's no use for me diving in.

00:38:49.930 --> 00:38:50.750
I better get a boat.

00:38:51.130 --> 00:38:53.270
Oh, hurry, officer, hurry.

00:38:54.330 --> 00:38:56.020
Did she do it?

00:38:56.700 --> 00:38:57.940
Ah, don't get excited.

00:38:58.230 --> 00:38:58.950
We'll save her.

00:38:59.030 --> 00:38:59.830
Oh, I know you won't.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.730
You know, eh? Are you her husband?

00:39:01.910 --> 00:39:02.570
No, let me go!

00:39:02.730 --> 00:39:04.970
Wait! Just who are you, anyway?

00:39:05.090 --> 00:39:06.490
Larry Stevens, Evening News.

00:39:13.700 --> 00:39:15.260
If I could swim, I'd do it, too.

00:39:15.460 --> 00:39:16.140
What was his name?

00:39:16.340 --> 00:39:17.520
Oh, Stevens, Evening News.

00:39:17.740 --> 00:39:19.320
What they won't do to get a story.

00:39:29.300 --> 00:39:29.660
Sylvia!

00:39:31.400 --> 00:39:36.130
Larry, what are you doing here? You've spoiled everything.

00:39:36.310 --> 00:39:37.890
Oh, Sylvia, darling, I knew you were in danger.

00:39:38.520 --> 00:39:41.040
I wasn't. I was just trying to save you.

00:39:41.360 --> 00:39:43.560
Well, it looks like we were both trying to save each other.

00:39:43.700 --> 00:39:55.240
I had to make a prediction, and then I had to make it look like it really happened.

00:39:55.540 --> 00:39:57.460
Oh, you wonderful, foolish little darling.

00:39:57.620 --> 00:39:59.350
Yes, but I didn't know.

00:39:59.470 --> 00:39:59.970
You didn't know why?

00:40:00.670 --> 00:40:02.900
That the water was so cold.

00:40:05.320 --> 00:40:06.720
Now I know the newspaper was wrong.

00:40:07.570 --> 00:40:07.970
Newspaper?

00:40:08.390 --> 00:40:08.890
Oh, never mind.

00:40:09.540 --> 00:40:10.500
You're here, alive.

00:40:10.520 --> 00:40:11.240
I found you.

00:40:19.720 --> 00:40:24.390
Oh, floating.

00:40:24.720 --> 00:40:27.080
Her hat, maybe, but the girl must have gone down like a stone.

00:40:28.420 --> 00:40:29.480
Let's go on further.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:33.640
Ah, no hurry. It'll be just another case of body not recovered.

00:40:33.900 --> 00:40:35.000
Did you hear that?

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:37.200
That's what I want them to think.

00:40:37.980 --> 00:40:39.260
Body not recovered.

00:40:40.150 --> 00:40:42.250
Gee hoes, if I get it, that'll be the headline.

00:40:42.780 --> 00:40:43.980
Not if they find me here.

00:40:44.140 --> 00:40:45.120
Don't worry, they won't.

00:40:45.200 --> 00:40:46.060
I know they won't.

00:41:08.030 --> 00:41:09.050
Now you can put me down.

00:41:09.370 --> 00:41:10.990
Oh, no, no, you're dripping wet.

00:41:11.360 --> 00:41:13.180
How could I explain a girl's facts in the hallway?

00:41:13.990 --> 00:41:14.530
Open the door.

00:41:28.780 --> 00:41:29.800
But you can come in now.

00:41:32.750 --> 00:41:34.170
Hey, you're just a little thing, aren't you?

00:41:34.720 --> 00:41:36.040
I feel perfectly silly.

00:41:36.220 --> 00:41:37.580
How can I go home like this?

00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:39.720
There's nobody on the street this time of night.

00:41:39.820 --> 00:41:41.120
And besides, you look very respectable.

00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:43.960
Don't even need a shave.

00:41:45.490 --> 00:41:46.110
It's not that you're tired.

00:41:46.580 --> 00:41:49.640
Oh, I nearly choked myself trying to tie it the way you do.

00:41:49.980 --> 00:41:50.660
Let me enjoy it.

00:41:51.850 --> 00:41:52.110
Ouch.

00:41:52.610 --> 00:41:52.950
Sorry.

00:41:53.690 --> 00:41:55.860
Now, look, you take both ends like this, see?

00:41:56.600 --> 00:41:57.580
And you put it right over left.

00:41:59.300 --> 00:41:59.900
No, you...

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:01.320
Cross left over right.

00:42:03.560 --> 00:42:04.460
I'm all mixed up.

00:42:04.910 --> 00:42:06.050
Why, no, it's backwards for me.

00:42:06.170 --> 00:42:06.430
Come over here.

00:42:09.380 --> 00:42:09.580
Better.

00:42:10.740 --> 00:42:11.300
Watch closely.

00:42:11.460 --> 00:42:13.700
You might have to do this for your husband someday.

00:42:16.000 --> 00:42:17.260
You know, on you, this suit looks good.

00:42:17.990 --> 00:42:18.830
It's the first time I've liked it.

00:42:20.740 --> 00:42:21.970
Sorry, I looked in the closet.

00:42:22.750 --> 00:42:23.810
Couldn't find a girl's dress.

00:42:24.050 --> 00:42:25.960
I should hope not.

00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:28.480
Matter of fact, I don't care.

00:42:29.540 --> 00:42:29.980
Well, I'm glad.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:36.280
you're not the jealous type would i be jealous of well if you cared at all i'd have to tell you

00:42:36.280 --> 00:42:44.240
that i'm a very busy character i haven't got time to be interested in girls oh last night in the cab

00:42:44.240 --> 00:42:52.700
you didn't act like a man who's not interested in girls last night great scott was it only last

00:42:52.700 --> 00:42:59.860
night we meant you mean to tell me all this

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:04.800
happened since last night sure I met the old man on the way home after I left you give me your

00:43:04.800 --> 00:43:10.580
newspaper I want to read it oh he didn't give it to me tonight he only read it to me well the old

00:43:10.580 --> 00:43:16.300
man was outside the window and I what's the use nobody believes this Larry you have a wonderful

00:43:16.300 --> 00:43:22.180
imagination you ought to join our act maybe you could read a number inside a watch say by the way

00:43:22.180 --> 00:43:29.100
how do you do that trick we magicians never reveal our secrets right Larry but I have no secrets I'm

00:43:29.100 --> 00:43:29.780
telling you the truth.

00:43:31.050 --> 00:43:34.690
last night when the old man gave me the paper I didn't even read it but this

00:43:34.690 --> 00:43:50.010
morning this is awful I fell asleep did you why didn't you wake me oh I guess I

00:43:50.010 --> 00:43:52.620
was dreaming too besides your shoes aren't dry yet

00:43:52.940 --> 00:43:56.540
oh I can't wait any longer I have to put them on

00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:06.230
Oh, darn. What do I do now?

00:44:10.480 --> 00:44:11.540
Oh, no, no, don't get out.

00:44:11.990 --> 00:44:13.530
Oh, please go. Don't stay here.

00:44:14.560 --> 00:44:15.080
What's the matter?

00:44:15.510 --> 00:44:16.110
Oh, my key.

00:44:16.330 --> 00:44:16.870
You lost it?

00:44:17.170 --> 00:44:18.990
I left it in my purse in the dressing room.

00:44:19.110 --> 00:44:19.750
What about your window?

00:44:20.260 --> 00:44:21.800
Oh, thank goodness I left that unlocked.

00:44:21.940 --> 00:44:22.580
Well, here, I'll help you.

00:44:22.660 --> 00:44:24.440
Oh, no, no, no, please. Please go.

00:44:25.230 --> 00:44:26.070
That man's watching.

00:44:26.360 --> 00:44:27.440
Are you sure you can make it?

00:44:27.540 --> 00:44:28.660
Oh, yes, yes. Good night.

00:44:30.060 --> 00:44:31.100
You can go now.

00:44:31.340 --> 00:44:31.800
Yes, sir.

00:44:32.920 --> 00:44:33.320
Good night.

00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:25.500
Miss O'Connor?

00:45:25.580 --> 00:45:26.260
Tis a burglar.

00:45:26.590 --> 00:45:28.330
I just seen him climb into Miss Sylvia's window.

00:45:30.190 --> 00:45:31.090
Did you call Sigalini?

00:45:31.400 --> 00:45:32.580
He's not in his room.

00:45:32.900 --> 00:45:34.980
Be careful with that thing. It might go off.

00:45:35.060 --> 00:45:36.580
I don't like the hamlet.

00:45:36.900 --> 00:45:37.440
Give it to me.

00:45:37.640 --> 00:45:37.920
Sure.

00:45:38.510 --> 00:45:40.570
Oh, a burglar. What are we going to do?

00:45:40.670 --> 00:45:42.390
Don't make a sound. Maybe he'll go away.

00:45:42.800 --> 00:45:45.580
He'll go a whole lot faster if we all scream for the police.

00:45:46.760 --> 00:45:48.740
You stay right here.

00:45:53.270 --> 00:45:54.450
I'll go find a policeman.

00:45:56.150 --> 00:45:56.950
I'm not afraid.

00:46:06.970 --> 00:46:09.020
Poor girl. She must still be asleep.

00:46:09.600 --> 00:46:10.600
Baby's threatening her.

00:46:12.420 --> 00:46:14.120
There's a light in the window. Look.

00:46:32.630 --> 00:46:35.470
Oh, these theatrical people, they're awful.

00:46:39.960 --> 00:46:41.000
Folks are up a bit late.

00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:43.540
We was waiting for you.

00:46:44.080 --> 00:46:44.760
Oh, well, thank you.

00:46:44.840 --> 00:46:46.140
That's mighty kind of you, dear ladies.

00:46:46.340 --> 00:46:48.480
But I was being entertained tonight

00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:50.740
by an old friend of mine, Inspector Mulroney.

00:46:51.160 --> 00:46:52.060
He wanted my advice.

00:46:52.780 --> 00:46:54.120
Tell me, have you seen my niece?

00:46:54.380 --> 00:46:55.200
Indeed, we have.

00:46:55.420 --> 00:46:56.080
I was a bit worried.

00:46:56.180 --> 00:46:57.040
She was kind of nervous tonight.

00:46:57.260 --> 00:46:57.520
Indeed?

00:46:57.930 --> 00:46:59.090
Yeah, she went off by herself.

00:46:59.230 --> 00:46:59.970
I guess she went the better...

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:02.580
Well, if she did, she got up again because we saw her at the window.

00:47:02.780 --> 00:47:04.620
Well, the poor girl's probably worried about me.

00:47:04.860 --> 00:47:05.780
I'll tell her I'm home.

00:47:07.230 --> 00:47:08.550
Sylvia, are you awake, dear?

00:47:08.910 --> 00:47:11.430
She'll not be answering your professor and you cooing like a pigeon.

00:47:11.640 --> 00:47:13.260
She must be awake if you saw at the window.

00:47:13.440 --> 00:47:14.540
That's not all I seen.

00:47:14.890 --> 00:47:15.830
I seen a man.

00:47:15.930 --> 00:47:17.110
And he's in there now.

00:47:30.160 --> 00:47:31.540
What is it, Uncle Oscar? What's wrong?

00:47:33.000 --> 00:47:35.980
Just some nosy people trying to scandalize your name. That's what's wrong.

00:47:36.180 --> 00:47:39.660
What do you mean saying there's a man in my niece's room?

00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:41.940
Just a bunch of scandal-mongers, that's what you are.

00:47:42.240 --> 00:47:45.560
They can be busted or an innocent young girl this time of the night and scared, I hear you.

00:47:58.580 --> 00:47:59.960
You're all liars! Now come in here!

00:48:01.040 --> 00:48:03.040
Look everywhere! Look in that closet!

00:48:03.380 --> 00:48:04.420
Look under that bed!

00:48:12.230 --> 00:48:17.020
Get out yourself!

00:48:18.150 --> 00:48:18.950
Come on, I see you!

00:48:19.030 --> 00:48:20.610
Get out from the bed or I'll pull you out!

00:48:33.360 --> 00:48:35.000
He can't run very fast without his shoes.

00:48:55.550 --> 00:48:55.830
Nico!

00:48:56.090 --> 00:48:56.450
Who?

00:48:56.550 --> 00:48:57.690
The fella jumped out that window!

00:48:57.890 --> 00:48:59.910
The guy that jumped out that window!

00:49:00.620 --> 00:49:02.300
Smart guy, come on!

00:49:02.320 --> 00:49:03.940
Wait a minute! Officer, let me...

00:49:03.940 --> 00:49:20.610
Have they found Stevens' body yet?

00:49:20.730 --> 00:49:22.150
They're still dragging the river.

00:49:23.190 --> 00:49:24.350
Sweeney, have you finished his obituary?

00:49:24.610 --> 00:49:25.090
Yes, sir.

00:49:26.500 --> 00:49:28.480
Refer to him as Lawrence Stevens, not Larry.

00:49:29.020 --> 00:49:29.740
Give it a little dignity.

00:49:30.120 --> 00:49:31.140
Cut it down, it's too long.

00:49:31.320 --> 00:49:31.680
Yes, sir.

00:49:32.910 --> 00:49:33.590
Any further details?

00:49:33.770 --> 00:49:35.110
