01:03:25.570 --> 01:03:26.290
Eden Gardens.

01:03:26.760 --> 01:03:28.120
All right, we'll go ourselves.

01:03:28.870 --> 01:03:29.970
No, we ain't going to...

01:03:31.020 --> 01:03:32.100
Get in, darling. This is for you.

01:03:32.260 --> 01:03:33.580
All right, driver, hurry up to the racetrack.

01:03:33.640 --> 01:03:35.240
I want to get there in time to make a bet in the first race.

01:03:35.420 --> 01:03:37.900
Now, the bike can help, but driver, don't pay no taxes to the bed.

01:03:38.000 --> 01:03:39.080
Take it to the eating gut.

01:03:39.300 --> 01:03:40.320
The man's crazy.

01:03:51.020 --> 01:03:53.500
Sorry, miss. There are no ladies permitted inside the betting ring.

01:03:53.640 --> 01:03:54.840
Good. Can you keep him out, too?

01:03:54.940 --> 01:03:55.440
Wait here, dear.

01:03:55.910 --> 01:03:57.150
Oh, I better go to the watch him.

01:04:09.660 --> 01:04:10.600
A hundred dollars on lamplighter.

01:04:11.150 --> 01:04:12.730
You wouldn't try to kid me, would you, mister?

01:04:12.990 --> 01:04:13.930
Lamplighter to win. Here's the hundred.

01:04:14.410 --> 01:04:17.330
Go on, peddle your papers. Lamplighter just won by two lengths.

01:04:19.620 --> 01:04:21.020
Well, did I know the winner or didn't I?

01:04:21.220 --> 01:04:23.960
Ah, that's just fool luck. I never knew a gambler yet that didn't go broke.

01:04:24.100 --> 01:04:26.180
But I'm not a gambler. I tell you, I can't lose.

01:04:26.700 --> 01:04:27.780
That's the spirit, mister.

01:04:28.080 --> 01:04:29.540
How about picking a winner for the second race?

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:30.640
Do you want me to tell you?

01:04:31.060 --> 01:04:31.380
Sure.

01:04:32.270 --> 01:04:32.590
Mudlock.

01:04:32.830 --> 01:04:33.730
The odds are 20 to 1.

01:04:33.870 --> 01:04:34.570
Do you want to lay that 100?

01:04:34.750 --> 01:04:35.210
Sure, sure.

01:04:35.350 --> 01:04:35.890
Take the wad.

01:04:35.930 --> 01:04:36.630
Teach him a lesson.

01:04:37.060 --> 01:04:39.580
The sooner he goes broke, the sooner he's going to find out this is a sucker game.

01:04:40.940 --> 01:04:49.560
I'm going to send you back to the boneyard, you...

01:04:49.560 --> 01:04:51.800
Oh, what a dog.

01:04:51.980 --> 01:04:53.360
He wouldn't even make good cat meat.

01:04:54.470 --> 01:04:54.790
Mudlock.

01:04:56.200 --> 01:04:56.520
Mudlock.

01:05:01.010 --> 01:05:04.630
Mudlock! Mudlock! Mudlock! Mudlock! He's in! Mudlock!

01:05:10.420 --> 01:05:12.660
Don't be afraid. The horses were slower, that's all.

01:05:15.040 --> 01:05:17.660
Two thousand dollars and my congratulations, sir.

01:05:17.880 --> 01:05:19.740
If I had your luck, friend, I'd ride it.

01:05:19.860 --> 01:05:22.160
That's just what I'm gonna do. Why'll you pay on lightning in the third?

01:05:22.320 --> 01:05:23.200
Straight place of show.

01:05:23.320 --> 01:05:25.000
For when? It's not for me, it's for Selvia.

01:05:25.160 --> 01:05:27.460
Then I'll take the money and go on home. She's my niece, ain't she?

01:05:27.660 --> 01:05:29.560
I got a right and a duty to protect the future.

01:05:30.000 --> 01:05:30.660
I'll take the witness, please.

01:05:30.960 --> 01:05:33.060
The other gentleman made the bet, my friend,

01:05:33.400 --> 01:05:34.780
the odds are five to one on lightning.

01:05:34.960 --> 01:05:35.380
What do you say?

01:05:35.500 --> 01:05:35.920
You're on.

01:05:36.020 --> 01:05:36.440
2,000.

01:05:36.740 --> 01:05:37.660
Spoken like a sport.

01:05:37.800 --> 01:05:38.980
Give the gentleman a ticket, Jerry.

01:05:39.280 --> 01:05:40.080
I can't stand it.

01:05:40.120 --> 01:05:40.940
I can't stand it.

01:05:41.040 --> 01:05:41.760
I won't say it.

01:05:41.920 --> 01:05:50.100
It can't be.

01:05:50.280 --> 01:05:50.800
It can't be.

01:05:50.880 --> 01:05:51.180
Lightning!

01:05:51.750 --> 01:05:52.350
Are you sure?

01:05:52.470 --> 01:05:52.830
Are you sure?

01:05:52.990 --> 01:05:53.930
Well, look for yourself.

01:06:01.370 --> 01:06:03.290
You mean you want to bet all this money on Ramona?

01:06:03.550 --> 01:06:04.370
Right, to win.

01:06:04.590 --> 01:06:05.690
I'll take Ramona, too.

01:06:05.870 --> 01:06:09.920
I'm afraid that will have to be an even money bet, mister.

01:06:10.600 --> 01:06:11.280
Give me that money.

01:06:11.360 --> 01:06:12.800
I get four to one in the place of this tent.

01:06:13.530 --> 01:06:14.350
You're a good customer.

01:06:14.510 --> 01:06:15.330
How about three to one?

01:06:16.010 --> 01:06:16.530
Three to one?

01:06:17.160 --> 01:06:17.380
OK.

01:06:18.030 --> 01:06:18.530
Wait a minute.

01:06:18.670 --> 01:06:19.550
These bread is for suckers.

01:06:19.590 --> 01:06:21.010
This way we can only win 30,000.

01:06:21.210 --> 01:06:22.110
If Ramona wins.

01:06:22.330 --> 01:06:23.130
Of course if Ramona win.

01:06:23.350 --> 01:06:24.270
Well, don't worry.

01:06:24.430 --> 01:06:25.110
Ramona will win.

01:06:26.380 --> 01:06:27.580
What is to be, will be.

01:06:39.310 --> 01:06:40.950
Look, Larry, Ramona's out ahead.

01:06:41.130 --> 01:06:42.230
I know.

01:06:42.470 --> 01:06:43.710
Isn't it wonderful, darling?

01:06:43.870 --> 01:06:45.590
Everything's turning out just the way you expect.

01:06:46.100 --> 01:06:46.500
Everything.

01:07:00.830 --> 01:07:02.690
It's a lot of money to bet on one horse, mister.

01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:04.410
I can't give you two to one on Black Flash.

01:07:04.960 --> 01:07:06.560
I can get you five to win on Diablo.

01:07:07.540 --> 01:07:08.160
Black Flash.

01:07:08.320 --> 01:07:09.280
Oh, don't be so pig-headed.

01:07:09.360 --> 01:07:10.280
What do you know about horses?

01:07:10.380 --> 01:07:11.040
Black Flash.

01:07:12.360 --> 01:07:14.820
You are $30,000 to win on Black Flash.

01:07:15.440 --> 01:07:17.520
For the love of Mike, would you put half it on Diablo?

01:07:17.720 --> 01:07:18.360
Black Flash.

01:07:19.400 --> 01:07:20.760
Been in this business a long time,

01:07:20.900 --> 01:07:23.340
but I never heard of anyone picking four sure things in a row.

01:07:23.860 --> 01:07:25.060
Not unless he's got things fixed.

01:07:26.490 --> 01:07:27.870
I think I'll do a little fixing myself.

01:07:29.210 --> 01:07:29.910
Diablo's going to win.

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:31.600
this time if he never runs another race.

01:07:45.920 --> 01:07:49.010
Diablo, Diablo, Diablo, Diablo...

01:08:03.100 --> 01:08:05.790
Get away from me. Get away from me, you and your tips.

01:08:05.970 --> 01:08:08.130
Well, they were wrong. They were wrong. Blackface lost.

01:08:08.600 --> 01:08:09.980
If I had my gun, I'd shoot you.

01:08:10.120 --> 01:08:11.120
But I'm not going to get shot.

01:08:11.180 --> 01:08:13.440
If the back page is wrong, the front page is going to be wrong.

01:08:13.680 --> 01:08:15.220
Sylvia, what a mess you've made out of your life.

01:08:15.300 --> 01:08:16.120
Look what you married.

01:08:16.340 --> 01:08:18.960
Oh, we're happy, Uncle. We're always going to be happy.

01:08:19.000 --> 01:08:20.240
Does anything else matter?

01:08:25.210 --> 01:08:29.100
The judges have the following official announcement to make.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:36.270
In the race which has just been run, number seven, Diablo has been disqualified.

01:08:36.960 --> 01:08:42.650
The winner in the fifth race is Black Flash.

01:08:44.290 --> 01:08:54.560
You are paying Mr. 60,000 simoleons. And don't give me them small bills.

01:08:54.720 --> 01:08:56.440
I hope you know this is gonna clean me out.

01:08:56.700 --> 01:08:59.200
Ha ha, I better you in a sucker's game. Ha ha!

01:09:00.670 --> 01:09:05.430
Oh, 49, 50, 51.

01:09:05.650 --> 01:09:06.390
Diver, stop.

01:09:06.650 --> 01:09:07.310
What's the matter?

01:09:07.470 --> 01:09:08.350
I'm not going back to town.

01:09:08.650 --> 01:09:09.750
Where else can we go?

01:09:09.910 --> 01:09:10.250
Anywhere.

01:09:10.750 --> 01:09:13.320
Well, we could have a nice dinner here in the country someplace.

01:09:13.700 --> 01:09:15.160
Oh, Larry, will you do something for me?

01:09:15.300 --> 01:09:15.920
Something nice.

01:09:16.500 --> 01:09:17.360
Let's be gay.

01:09:17.760 --> 01:09:20.720
I'd like to have dinner someplace where there's music and people.

01:09:21.860 --> 01:09:22.200
I know.

01:09:22.640 --> 01:09:23.680
The St. George Hotel.

01:09:24.580 --> 01:09:25.940
No, no, not tonight, darling.

01:09:26.440 --> 01:09:28.880
All right, Larry, we'll go tomorrow night, some other time.

01:09:29.200 --> 01:09:29.960
Here you are, my dear.

01:09:30.280 --> 01:09:31.360
This makes you a rich woman.

01:09:32.300 --> 01:09:34.060
No, I'd be afraid to carry that much money.

01:09:35.430 --> 01:09:36.510
You better keep it. It'll be safer.

01:09:36.760 --> 01:09:37.860
Oh, no, I might lose it.

01:09:38.020 --> 01:09:39.700
Well, what about me? Please take it.

01:09:40.020 --> 01:09:41.320
Well, somebody's got to take it.

01:09:42.780 --> 01:09:44.850
Stop! Leave! After him!

01:09:46.530 --> 01:09:52.420
After him! Leave! Leave! Stop!

01:09:53.580 --> 01:09:56.280
Pass the passenger drive. He's got $60,000 of our money.

01:09:56.460 --> 01:09:57.460
He's got a gun, too!

01:09:57.720 --> 01:09:59.180
Gun? Who cares?

01:09:59.400 --> 01:09:59.980
Sure, who...

01:10:05.200 --> 01:10:10.750
Get him out of here.

01:10:11.180 --> 01:10:13.340
You're wasting my time with your shenanigans.

01:10:13.760 --> 01:10:14.660
Shenanigans, my foot.

01:10:14.800 --> 01:10:16.520
I'm telling you, we chased the guys all the way into town.

01:10:16.700 --> 01:10:18.100
Then he arrests us for speeding.

01:10:18.420 --> 01:10:20.140
Why did you chase the guy that was stealing our money?

01:10:20.240 --> 01:10:21.220
It was over $60,000.

01:10:22.240 --> 01:10:22.960
$60,000.

01:10:23.060 --> 01:10:23.440
Go on.

01:10:23.540 --> 01:10:24.500
Who do you think I am?

01:10:24.700 --> 01:10:25.980
That's a fine police force.

01:10:26.180 --> 01:10:28.000
You let the thief escape and you arrest the victim.

01:10:28.060 --> 01:10:28.720
Come on, beat it.

01:10:28.800 --> 01:10:29.200
Beat it.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:31.740
Now, wait a minute. You can't throw me out of jail. I'm arrested.

01:10:32.020 --> 01:10:33.720
Lock me up and don't let me out of here before tomorrow.

01:10:34.020 --> 01:10:36.200
Get out of here, both of you. I'm sick of you.

01:10:37.050 --> 01:10:38.930
Inspector, lock me up for just a half an hour.

01:10:39.360 --> 01:10:39.880
What for?

01:10:40.160 --> 01:10:41.580
Well, I'm arrested. Put me in jail.

01:10:42.280 --> 01:10:45.580
Jail? Where you belong is the bug house. Get him out of here.

01:10:46.600 --> 01:10:47.420
Oh, wait a minute.

01:10:47.540 --> 01:10:48.720
Inspector, do me a favor, will you?

01:10:49.120 --> 01:10:51.140
Just lock me up here for 35 minutes.

01:10:51.400 --> 01:10:51.620
Yeah.

01:10:51.740 --> 01:10:52.400
You don't know what it means.

01:10:52.460 --> 01:10:55.040
Get out of here and stay out.

01:11:12.890 --> 01:11:14.510
I wonder why he didn't want us to go in there with him.

01:11:15.390 --> 01:11:17.950
Maybe he had some personal business to attend to, Uncle.

01:11:18.210 --> 01:11:18.950
Oh, yeah, yeah.

01:11:19.110 --> 01:11:20.870
The fella must be in there who gives him all the winners.

01:11:21.240 --> 01:11:22.100
I hope he finds them.

01:11:27.140 --> 01:11:28.040
Where you been all day?

01:11:28.140 --> 01:11:29.840
Yeah, the boss is tearing his hair.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:31.760
Looking all over town for his number one reporter.

01:11:31.880 --> 01:11:32.180
Here, listen.

01:11:32.460 --> 01:11:33.800
Have any of you fellows seen Pop Benson?

01:11:36.890 --> 01:11:37.810
What's the matter? Where is he?

01:11:38.520 --> 01:11:39.760
You mean you haven't heard?

01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:40.460
Heard what?

01:11:41.070 --> 01:11:43.040
Why, the old man is dead.

01:11:43.780 --> 01:11:43.980
Dead?

01:11:44.850 --> 01:11:45.930
I'm writing his obit.

01:11:46.980 --> 01:11:47.320
What caused it?

01:11:47.730 --> 01:11:49.290
Just old age, I guess.

01:11:50.580 --> 01:11:51.440
When did you last see him?

01:11:51.620 --> 01:11:52.920
We all saw him, Larry.

01:11:53.140 --> 01:11:53.840
You were here.

01:11:54.150 --> 01:11:54.410
When?

01:11:54.780 --> 01:11:55.800
Well, three nights ago.

01:11:56.210 --> 01:11:57.730
He died just after we left him.

01:11:58.830 --> 01:11:59.490
You remember?

01:12:00.160 --> 01:12:01.700
We were all kidding in the library.

01:12:01.940 --> 01:12:03.580
Remember how we all laughed when he said,

01:12:03.940 --> 01:12:05.620
How do you know you've got 10 years to live?

01:12:05.780 --> 01:12:06.600
Poor old fella.

01:12:07.030 --> 01:12:09.550
Good thing he didn't know he only had time to get home himself.

01:12:10.410 --> 01:12:11.730
Oh, don't take it so hard, Larry.

01:12:12.090 --> 01:12:14.710
When they found the old man, they said he had a smile on his face.

01:12:14.930 --> 01:12:16.890
Sure. He was always happy.

01:12:17.860 --> 01:12:19.920
Remember how he always tried to play jokes on people?

01:12:20.040 --> 01:12:20.380
Yeah.

01:12:21.430 --> 01:12:22.900
Stephen, come in here.

01:12:25.700 --> 01:12:26.500
Look at that clock.

01:12:27.140 --> 01:12:28.040
Ten past six.

01:12:28.830 --> 01:12:29.970
How long do you expect...

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:35.180
to hold down your job not very long mr. Gordon right but I'm going to give you

01:12:35.180 --> 01:12:39.000
another chance I have an overnight assignment for you I can't make it I

01:12:39.000 --> 01:12:44.360
have an appointment at 625 cancel it I'll do my best I got a tip something big

01:12:44.360 --> 01:12:47.900
is going to break I'll give you the address never mind I I know where it is

01:12:48.440 --> 01:12:54.620
where St. George Hotel St. George Hotel that's not it the other side of town you

01:12:54.680 --> 01:12:59.210
mean you're not sending me to the St. George Hotel can't you read mr. Gordon

01:12:59.210 --> 01:12:59.970
aren't you making a mistake

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:02.420
Am I in the habit of making mistakes, young man?

01:13:02.640 --> 01:13:04.140
Now you get in the cab and get over there right away.

01:13:05.310 --> 01:13:05.750
All right.

01:13:07.170 --> 01:13:09.210
But I'm afraid I'm going to wind up at the St. George Hotel

01:13:09.210 --> 01:13:11.110
at 625, no matter where I go.

01:13:13.440 --> 01:13:14.440
St. George Hotel?

01:13:16.290 --> 01:13:16.750
I don't know.

01:13:16.850 --> 01:13:18.170
Maybe there's something wrong somewhere.

01:13:18.410 --> 01:13:19.390
It's in a different direction.

01:13:19.760 --> 01:13:20.740
It's in the opposite direction.

01:13:23.750 --> 01:13:27.300
Stephens, forget that assignment I gave you.

01:13:27.680 --> 01:13:29.520
Go to the St. George Hotel.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:33.760
Oh, you know what for, my boy, you've got the best nose for news in this town.

01:13:33.980 --> 01:13:37.320
If you said St. George Hotel, you had a reason to say St. George Hotel.

01:13:37.580 --> 01:13:39.760
You can't fool me. I know where your apartment is.

01:13:39.920 --> 01:13:42.700
It's 6.15 now. Hurry up. I don't want you to be late.

01:13:46.590 --> 01:13:48.700
Stick around, boys. We're getting out an extra.

01:13:50.200 --> 01:13:52.160
You mean to say that we ain't going to get no more tips?

01:13:52.400 --> 01:13:55.240
Oh, I don't care. We'll get along. Larry has a job.

01:13:55.820 --> 01:13:59.970
What time is it? Time? 6...

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:00.980
It can't be.

01:14:01.590 --> 01:14:02.930
Well, my watch may be slow.

01:14:03.460 --> 01:14:04.460
Driver, what time you got?

01:14:05.210 --> 01:14:06.250
Twenty after six, sir.

01:14:06.450 --> 01:14:07.810
Don't be so nervous, dear.

01:14:07.930 --> 01:14:08.790
We've plenty of time.

01:14:08.990 --> 01:14:10.210
Sure, we're almost there.

01:14:10.330 --> 01:14:10.530
Where?

01:14:10.920 --> 01:14:11.920
The St. George Hotel.

01:14:12.370 --> 01:14:13.310
Who said St. George Hotel?

01:14:13.630 --> 01:14:14.130
You did!

01:14:14.410 --> 01:14:15.630
That's what you said when you got this camp.

01:14:15.730 --> 01:14:17.290
St. George Hotel, St. George Hotel.

01:14:17.570 --> 01:14:19.290
You knew I wanted to have our wedding party there.

01:14:19.310 --> 01:14:20.490
Driver, driver, stop, stop.

01:14:20.770 --> 01:14:22.090
Turn around, go the other way, quick.

01:14:22.310 --> 01:14:23.150
No, hold it, hold it.

01:14:23.210 --> 01:14:23.690
I'll get out here.

01:14:24.140 --> 01:14:24.500
Larry!

01:14:24.740 --> 01:14:26.860
So, darling, don't argue, please, if you love me.

01:14:27.240 --> 01:14:28.980
First you want to go to the St. George Hotel,

01:14:29.120 --> 01:14:29.980
now you don't want to go.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:30.740
to the St. George O'Call.

01:14:30.760 --> 01:14:31.640
What's my fare, mister?

01:14:31.880 --> 01:14:33.260
Oh, you'll have to pay the cabbie.

01:14:33.360 --> 01:14:35.280
I left all my money in my wallet, and the thief took it.

01:14:35.460 --> 01:14:36.520
Is camp a hire, driver?

01:14:36.660 --> 01:14:37.620
Will be when I get paid.

01:15:33.610 --> 01:15:36.000
Stay where you are. This time you're gonna get enough of me.

01:15:36.120 --> 01:15:37.200
This is in the St. George Hotel.

01:16:20.920 --> 01:16:22.220
You don't think a fall can kill me, do you?

01:18:09.240 --> 01:18:11.480
Have you seen a man in a great sex suit?

01:18:11.600 --> 01:18:12.660
He's been running away from me.

01:18:12.800 --> 01:18:13.600
Duck, you fool!

01:18:13.780 --> 01:18:14.440
He's shooting at us!

01:18:15.580 --> 01:18:16.200
I'll get him.

01:18:16.540 --> 01:18:16.960
Get down!

01:18:17.260 --> 01:18:17.980
Get down!

01:18:37.070 --> 01:18:37.330
Hands up.

01:18:38.820 --> 01:18:39.280
Get up.

01:19:00.510 --> 01:19:23.250
Who is he, Mac?

01:19:30.120 --> 01:19:32.830
Lawrence Stevens, Evening News.

01:19:33.780 --> 01:19:35.100
What? What?

01:19:36.230 --> 01:19:39.650
Stevens? Yes, I sent him to St. George Hotel myself.

01:19:40.780 --> 01:19:41.500
A few minutes ago.

01:19:41.760 --> 01:19:44.170
Huh? Well, no. No, the man was on duty.

01:19:45.060 --> 01:19:45.880
The man's a hero.

01:19:46.640 --> 01:19:49.040
He knew something big was going to happen to the St. George Hotel.

01:19:49.410 --> 01:19:50.210
Hello. Hello!

01:19:50.630 --> 01:19:51.670
What's happened, Mr. Gordon?

01:19:52.870 --> 01:19:53.630
Tell the press room.

01:19:54.020 --> 01:19:55.460
We're getting out an extra. Hold everything.

01:19:55.850 --> 01:19:57.850
Hop over to the St. George Hotel. They just shot Stevens.

01:19:57.950 --> 01:19:58.670
Hurry up. Hurry up.

01:19:59.580 --> 01:19:59.980
Take this...

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:06.310
Barry Stevens, Evening News reporter, shot to death in the lobby of St. George Utero.

01:20:08.100 --> 01:20:16.540
Side, everybody. Go on, outside.

01:20:16.920 --> 01:20:17.220
What happened?

01:20:17.500 --> 01:20:19.740
Nothing, nothing. Some newspaper guy was killed, that's all.

01:20:19.840 --> 01:20:20.220
Who was it?

01:20:21.360 --> 01:20:22.980
Harry something, Harry...

01:20:22.980 --> 01:20:23.320
Stevens?

01:20:23.660 --> 01:20:25.060
Yeah, Stevens. Now go on, get out.

01:20:36.400 --> 01:20:37.590
Here, where are you going?

01:20:37.690 --> 01:20:38.250
Evening news.

01:20:38.450 --> 01:20:38.870
All right, go ahead.

01:20:40.820 --> 01:20:41.120
Barry!

01:20:43.120 --> 01:20:43.280
Barry!

01:20:43.780 --> 01:20:45.180
You're supposed to be dead!

01:20:45.640 --> 01:20:46.950
Yeah, I know.

01:20:47.470 --> 01:20:48.330
They say I am.

01:20:48.490 --> 01:20:50.080
What do you think?

01:20:50.800 --> 01:20:51.600
You're alive!

01:20:53.410 --> 01:20:54.230
This is terrible.

01:20:59.530 --> 01:20:59.970
That's not a problem.

01:21:00.500 --> 01:21:01.860
Get me the evening news, quick.

01:21:04.180 --> 01:21:04.540
Inspector.

01:21:05.900 --> 01:21:08.200
Inspector, for Pete's sakes, tell me, what happened?

01:21:08.340 --> 01:21:09.120
What am I doing here?

01:21:09.920 --> 01:21:11.320
I've already told you.

01:21:11.660 --> 01:21:13.680
I'm getting awful sick of you, Stevens.

01:21:14.780 --> 01:21:15.360
Is this yours?

01:21:16.010 --> 01:21:16.290
Yeah.

01:21:16.880 --> 01:21:19.240
Then how did it get in the pocket of the man who was killed?

01:21:21.520 --> 01:21:22.260
I get it.

01:21:22.510 --> 01:21:23.110
I get it!

01:21:23.290 --> 01:21:23.850
Well, answer me!

01:21:23.930 --> 01:21:25.390
Inspector, you're a wonderful man.

01:21:25.510 --> 01:21:26.090
I love you.

01:21:26.150 --> 01:21:27.050
May I see you so bad?

01:21:27.150 --> 01:21:27.670
I'm alive.

01:21:27.670 --> 01:21:28.230
I'm alive.

01:21:28.410 --> 01:21:28.950
It's wonderful.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:36.360
Our extra, with your death story, is on the streets.

01:21:43.000 --> 01:21:46.590
Order shot today to get your papers!

01:21:49.510 --> 01:21:50.150
Extra, sir?

01:21:52.090 --> 01:21:53.090
No, thanks, I've got it.

01:21:53.450 --> 01:21:54.250
This just came out.

01:21:54.700 --> 01:21:55.420
That's all right.

01:21:55.900 --> 01:21:56.860
I can live without it.

01:21:58.740 --> 01:21:59.980
What I'd like to know is what happened.

01:22:00.700 --> 01:22:03.520
Oh, who cares? Didn't seem real anyway.

01:22:04.170 --> 01:22:06.210
That's right. Came in like a dream, went out like a dream.

01:22:06.390 --> 01:22:07.850
That racetrack ain't no dream, no?

01:22:08.160 --> 01:22:09.720
It's a man's assist to clean up millions.

01:22:09.900 --> 01:22:10.780
All you gotta do is pick them.

01:22:10.920 --> 01:22:13.000
That's all. Good night.

01:22:13.270 --> 01:22:13.910
Good night, kids.

01:22:14.540 --> 01:22:20.040
You interested in horse racing?

01:22:20.220 --> 01:22:23.610
I don't play sure things.

01:22:23.730 --> 01:22:24.750
You must have a good system.

01:22:24.970 --> 01:22:25.650
You said it, friend.

01:22:25.890 --> 01:22:27.530
Just come around tomorrow, and I'll show you how it's done.

01:22:27.750 --> 01:22:28.650
It's very simple.

01:22:29.300 --> 01:22:29.960
All you do is pick...

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:33.780
the money that you win on the first race and you bet it on the winner in the second race then you

01:22:33.780 --> 01:22:37.000
take the money that you won on the second race and you bet it on the winner in the third race

01:22:37.000 --> 01:22:40.760
and then you don't lose your nerves see but you take the whole bundle and you put it on the winner

01:22:40.760 --> 01:22:51.260
in the fourth race cab cab all right darling we can't take a cab why not we haven't any money

01:22:51.260 --> 01:22:57.480
oh well i guess we'll just have to wait here till the rain stops poor darling what a wedding night

01:22:57.480 --> 01:22:59.920
No money, no cab, no umbrella, no shelter.

01:23:00.820 --> 01:23:02.520
Nothing but a wonderful future.

01:23:03.140 --> 01:23:04.620
Don't tell them you could read the future.

01:23:04.780 --> 01:23:06.080
Let's always take life as it comes.

01:23:06.620 --> 01:23:09.300
Larry, darling, I only pretended to read the future.

01:23:09.610 --> 01:23:10.950
We had to in our act.

01:23:11.900 --> 01:23:16.110
Oh, but when I'm close to you, I really feel I can look way ahead.

01:23:16.810 --> 01:23:17.770
Years and years.

01:23:18.470 --> 01:23:19.920
What do you see? Are we happy?

01:23:20.160 --> 01:23:22.260
We'll always be happy as long as we're together.

01:23:22.740 --> 01:23:23.840
Just the two of us.

01:23:24.200 --> 01:23:25.120
Just the two of us?

01:23:25.640 --> 01:23:27.620
Oh, no, I want at least four sons.

01:23:27.920 --> 01:23:28.760
Fine, fine.

01:23:31.120 --> 01:23:32.640
It'll have to be a big house.

01:23:32.740 --> 01:23:33.640
Oh, bigger than that.

01:23:33.900 --> 01:23:35.560
I wonder how he can afford it.

01:23:36.250 --> 01:23:38.270
He'll be the owner of the evening news.

01:23:38.430 --> 01:23:40.130
Well, then we can have a whole house full of children.

01:23:40.330 --> 01:23:41.670
Oh, big enough for grandchildren.

01:23:41.910 --> 01:23:43.110
And great-grandchildren someday.

01:23:43.900 --> 01:23:47.700
They can almost see them 50 years from tonight.

01:23:48.110 --> 01:23:50.320
It'll be our golden anniversary.

01:24:11.932 --> 01:24:12.232
I'm done.

01:24:13.692 --> 01:24:14.692
There we go.

01:24:17.308 --> 01:24:18.148
Thanks, Bob.

01:24:18.364 --> 01:24:19.324
It's good for something anyway.
